frsqrte-fres.patch -- PoC: scalar __builtin_frsqrte/__builtin_fres for the
GameCube backend (SN BUILD v1.79 source), imitating the fnmsubs define_insn
of rs6000.md:3668 and the __builtin_ps_* machinery of rs6000.c/rs6000.h.

The dossier (docs/asm-de-ea.md, bSqrt) shows the 86 GameCube functions that
expand bSqrt need frsqrte + fmuls + fnmsubs per Newton step, and that SN's
rs6000.md has no pattern for frsqrte/fres: the original is asm of EA.
fmuls comes from plain C (mulsf3); fnmsubs does NOT survive -ffast-math
(GCC folds -(a*b-c) to c-a*b, which has no pattern), so this PoC alone is
expected to leave the fnmsubs sites; the full plan adds an fnmsubs-minus
pattern/builtin on top. fres covers the eRecip site of eMathE.cpp.

What it does: two SFmode unspec define_insns (70/71, free: the tree uses
0-69) emitting frsqrte/fres under TARGET_POWERPC && TARGET_HARD_FLOAT;
two GEK_BUILTIN codes + a float->float bdesc table + an SF expander with
no Rc operand; MD_INIT_BUILTINS always inits (the PS builtins keep their
-mps-float gate inside gek_init_builtins). Applies to both source-built
toolchains (3.9.3-src, 3.9.3-v183src); build.sh's generator run takes the
union of patches so insn-codes.h sees the new patterns. Reference SHAs in
build.sh do not apply to patched builds; validate by .s comparison.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.md
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.md
@@ -3682,6 +3682,23 @@
   "! TARGET_POWERPC && TARGET_HARD_FLOAT && TARGET_FUSED_MADD"
   "{fnms|fnmsub} %0,%1,%2,%3"
   [(set_attr "type" "dmul")])
+
+;; Scalar single-precision estimates for __builtin_frsqrte/__builtin_fres
+;; (SN-PoC): imitate the fnmsubs define_insn above.  unspec keeps the
+;; estimate from being folded or CSE'd like an exact operation.
+(define_insn "b_frsqrtesf2"
+  [(set (match_operand:SF 0 "gpc_reg_operand" "=f")
+	(unspec:SF [(match_operand:SF 1 "gpc_reg_operand" "f")] 70))]
+  "TARGET_POWERPC && TARGET_HARD_FLOAT"
+  "frsqrte %0,%1"
+  [(set_attr "type" "fp")])
+
+(define_insn "b_fressf2"
+  [(set (match_operand:SF 0 "gpc_reg_operand" "=f")
+	(unspec:SF [(match_operand:SF 1 "gpc_reg_operand" "f")] 71))]
+  "TARGET_POWERPC && TARGET_HARD_FLOAT"
+  "fres %0,%1"
+  [(set_attr "type" "fp")])
 
 (define_expand "sqrtsf2"
   [(set (match_operand:SF 0 "gpc_reg_operand" "")
